    "group": "PGL(2,p\u00b2) \u2264 Aut(Paley conference of order p\u00b2+1) acting on PG(1,p\u00b2) \u2245 vertex set",
    "stabilizer_fact": "For every 4-set S={\u221e,0,1,\u03bb} (\u03bb\u2209{0,1,\u221e}), the setwise stabilizer in PGL(2,p\u00b2) contains the Klein four-group V4 generated by the double-transposition involutions (e.g. z\u21a6\u03bb/z swaps \u221e\u21940, 1\u2194\u03bb). V4 acts regularly on S, hence transitively.",
    "equivariance_tau1": "star_a \u03c41(a) is built from C-edge labels of S and of one-vertex extensions S_a\u2192r. Any g\u2208Aut(C) satisfies star_{ga} \u03c41(ga; gS) = star_a \u03c41(a; S). Restricting to g\u2208Stab_{setwise}(S) yields star_{ga} \u03c41(ga) = star_a \u03c41(a) for all a\u2208S; transitivity \u21d2 constant on a\u2208S.",
    "equivariance_S1": "Max+ = {y\u2208{\u00b11}^n : C y = p y} is Aut(C)-invariant. Hence m4(S)=E[\u220f_{i\u2208S} y_i] is Aut-invariant as a function of S, and star_a S1(a) (which depends on C and m4 on extensions of S) is Aut-equivariant. Same stabilizer argument \u21d2 constant on a\u2208S.",
    "scope": "Paley conference of order p\u00b2+1 (prime p). Constancy is for each fixed 4-set across its four centres \u2014 not constancy across sets.",
    "identity_t1": "On R1={r\u2209S:|\u03ba(S_a\u2192r)|=1}, let A=#{r\u2208R1: C_ar \u03ba'=+1}, B=#{r\u2208R1: C_ar \u03ba'=\u22121}, A+B=d1^(1)=(3p\u00b2-7)/4. Then \u03c41=A\u2212B=2A\u2212d1^(1), so star\u00b7\u03c41=star\u00b7(2A\u2212d1^(1))."
